{"step_index":2976,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T15:15:37Z","thinking":"Analyzing the CSS, it appears status badges use color-coding to represent different states (completed, reviewing, error, processing). The color scheme utilizes background and text color combinations to visually distinguish these states. This suggests a visual indicator is being used to communicate the status of an item.\n\n\nThe code indicates that submitting a process while a worker thread is active results in the process being queued. The queue implementation uses a lock to manage access and updates the database to reflect the new \"queued\" status. The worker thread then handles the process from the queue. An exception handler exists within the worker function to catch and log any errors.\n\n\nWhen an error occurs during process execution, the code dispatches a 'process\\_complete' event to the UI, including the error message. The code then checks if there are any queued processes. If so, it starts the next process and updates the database. The UI should display the updated process status. Specifically, a 'process\\_update' event is dispatched to the UI.\n\n\nUpon process completion, the UI should immediately reflect the updated status, including queued items. Adding a UI refresh call ensures the history screen is current after any process completion. A further update event will be dispatched when a queued process transitions to processing to ensure the UI updates the history table immediately with the current status of each process.\n\n\nUpon receiving the `process_queued_started` event, the UI should update process history and display a notification to the user. This will improve user experience by providing clear feedback on queued process starts. Examining the `rerun_process` function reveals that attempting to rerun a process while another is active results in an error, suggesting no queuing support in that specific function. This needs further examination.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"lines = open('desktop_app/templates/index.html', encoding='utf-8').readlines(); [print(i+1, l.strip()) for i, l in enumerate(lines) if 'rerun' in l.lower()]\"","Cwd":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Finding rerun in index.html","toolSummary":"Find rerun references in index.html"}}]}
